{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>בַּעֲבוּר etc. — וּלְמַעַן סַפֵּר.</b> It intends <b>בַּעֲבוּר הַרְאוֹתְךָ אֶת כֹּחִי</b> — you who said מִי ה׳ — <b>וּלְמַעַן סַפֵּר שְׁמִי</b> through you <b>בְּכָל הָאָרֶץ</b>; its meaning is that the entire world will recount the greatness of what He did to the refuser through His words. And so we heard that a certain great king said that if the Messiah of Israel should come and perform a sign or wonder, he would not refuse the word of HaShem as Pharaoh did."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "Reading לַמְּמָאֵן ('to the refuser') and לְמָאֵן ('refuse') as the same root מאן, 'to refuse/refuse,' matching Pharaoh's denial in context."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:26:06.577028821Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}